```c
// hello.c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    printf("Hello from ARM Linux!\n");
    return 0;
}
```
Command:
```bash
arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc \
    --sysroot=/opt/arm-toolchain/sysroot \
    -o hello_arm hello.c
```
Here, `arm-linux-gnueabihf-gcc` is the cross-compiler, and `--sysroot` points to the directory containing ARM-specific headers and libraries.
